## Context

The 2026-09-02 rendering ruling makes declared language renderings one answer
row. Collapse happens before the cut to k and only for twin attachments or an
explicit relation; similarity never silently merges records. The best-scoring
rendering leads and the others remain structured alternates.

## Actions

1. Derive a work/rendering group from twin attachments and explicit relations.
2. Collapse each declared group after entry collapse and before top-k.
3. Preserve the best-scoring rendering as the ranked hit.
4. Return other renderings as `{language, key}` alternates and render
   `also in: <lang> (<key>)` where a textual row is required.

## Test

- Two declared renderings occupy one row and free the displaced top-k slot.
- Two highly similar but unlinked records remain two rows.
- A query in one language does not replace a better-scoring rendering in
  another language.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Declared renderings collapse before top-k; inferred ones do not.
- [ ] Ranking follows the best-scoring rendering only.
- [ ] Structured alternates carry language and key.
- [ ] `make check` and `./tickets/erg check` pass.
